nd ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-7\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-7\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)={x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n{{{x}_{2}(t)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\"." 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371883 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371884 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371885 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371886 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371887 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1041 "selection" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371886 13194139535876 true] [17592186371882 1110 #uuid "7f985b96-21e2-5ec1-af64-3823f90be05f" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371883 1034 "I only" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535876 true] [17592186371883 1111 #uuid "0c0dee42-1c99-5d8d-b851-d147047f0b5a" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371884 1034 "III only" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535876 true] [17592186371884 1111 #uuid "ff3e1548-961f-58cc-91da-f89e1d1661ef" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371885 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535876 true] [17592186371885 1111 #uuid "789777b4-9f87-5a47-a72e-fceb61905319" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371886 1034 "I, II and III" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535876 true] [17592186371886 1111 #uuid "83a8a3d0-7014-5fc9-9a3f-c57cb66bff6d" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371887 1034 "II only" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535876 true] [17592186371887 1111 #uuid "c416c1d0-34f1-5f99-8a4a-2276986e9c2d" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371888 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371889 13194139535876 true] [17592186371888 1089 "q-76597" 13194139535876 true] [17592186371888 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535876 true] [17592186371888 1100 "If $\\,u(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,v(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are solutions to ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$, find $Aw(t)$ where $w(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194